--
N5008 [temp.param]/12-14 + [temp.arg.general]/1: a default template
argument given on a forward declaration (`template <class _CharT, class
_InIter = It<_CharT>> struct num_get;`, libstdc++'s <bits/localefwd.h>)
is substituted with THIS template's preceding parameters bound to the
preceding arguments.  The raw default was applied through the full
template map, whose short-name bridge bound `_CharT` to a same-named
parameter of an ENCLOSING instantiation (numpunct<char>::probe naming
num_get<wchar_t>): the hybrid num_get<wchar_t, It<char>> resulted --
~130 bogus facet instantiations per <regex> TU, and which existed
depended on candidate order.  The kernel places the enclosing template
before the definition so its parameter scope sorts first.
